gle (3) now, and planning to play the higher triplet (10-10-10) with the remaining single (9) later, you can transform your hand into a set of pairs (44, 66, 88, KK, AA, 22). With the top three ranks of pairs (KK, AA, 22) in hand, you will have immense control in the endgame. Playing the pair sequence (44-55-66) or full houses would strip your hand of structure but leave you with isolated singles, which are harder to defend.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥3", "♠5", "♣5", "♦5"]}'}
