ore efficient than playing a Triple with a single (clearing only 1 card, the 9). The remaining hand (66, 88, 9, KK, AA) contains high defensive pairs (KK, AA) to regain control.\n\nReason: The move 10-10-10-4-4 is the dominant play because 10-10-10 is the highest remaining triple, guaranteeing the trick (unless a Rocket is used). It clears the low pair of 4s, which is better than clearing the single 9, as it removes two weak cards instead of one.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠4", "♥4", "♠10", "♥10", "♣10"]}'}
